  "live_records": {
    "q-112760": {
      "dom_id": "step-q112760",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Given that $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{5}{6}),$ what is $\\text{SD}[X]?$",
      "worked_solution": "If $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\lambda )$ is an exponential random variable, then\n\n$$\n\\text{SD}[X]=\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[X]}=\\frac{1}{\\lambda }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, for our random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{5}{6}),$ we have the following standard deviation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{SD}[X] & =\\frac{1}{(\\frac{5}{6})} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
